{
  "id": "multi-phase-resume-events",
  "description": "Artifact-only resume rule (SKILL.md section 4): a graph step of the current phase_cursor is complete only if a result_persisted event for its agent and task phase carries details.phase_id equal to the phase_cursor and sits AFTER the latest phase_started or remediation_created event for that phase id (file order). The flat results slots hold the latest value of an EARLIER phase or REM-FIX cycle in both cases below, so a results-based check would wrongly skip the reviewer, the hunter and the verifier. Further cases: a no-plan BUILD compares null, missing and N/A phase ids as equal; an advisory pass that returned NEEDS_INFO or NEEDS_GRILLING does not complete its step (a second pass of the same agent and task phase follows), while CANDIDATES_FOUND does; locator_cases check the artifact-only lookup of a paused workflow by pending_gate for a bare reply (terminal artifacts dropped first, exactly one candidate answers its gate, more than one asks which, none starts a new workflow). The stop-state hint is not modelled: it names an artifact already in the scan.",
